From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] And fix linking

The X11 and Wayland drivers reference SDL_GetAppID, SDL_IOReady and
SDL_Zenity_ShowMessageBox, which live in src/core/unix and
src/dialog/unix; upstream only compiles those in if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
sections.  Add them whenever either driver is enabled - keying this on
SDL_COCOA (as before) broke the link as soon as Cocoa was enabled next
to X11/Wayland, since Cocoa neither needs nor provides these symbols.

---
diff --git CMakeLists.txt CMakeLists.txt
index 0f78f0bc4..76dd4b2bf 100644
--- CMakeLists.txt
+++ CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2517,6 +2517,17 @@ elseif(APPLE)
     set(HAVE_SDL_MAIN_CALLBACKS TRUE)
   endif()
 
+  # The X11 and Wayland drivers need these Unix helpers, which the generic
+  # if(UNIX) sections skip on Apple platforms; Cocoa neither needs nor
+  # provides them, so key this on the drivers rather than on SDL_COCOA.
+  if(SDL_X11 OR SDL_WAYLAND)
+    sdl_sources(
+      "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/core/unix/SDL_appid.c"
+      "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/core/unix/SDL_poll.c"
+      "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/dialog/unix/SDL_zenitymessagebox.c"
+    )
+  endif()
+
   if(SDL_CAMERA)
     if(MACOS OR IOS)
       set(SDL_CAMERA_DRIVER_COREMEDIA 1)
